=== the alpha^2 DERIVED (power-counting): two EM vertices linking the dark fields ===
  dCDF <-> electron : light is the dCDF Goldstone -> couples to e-charge at EM strength ~ alpha
  dyad <-> electron : varying-m_e, eps = 27 alpha/5pi -> coupling ~ alpha_c = 3 alpha ~ alpha
  handshake dyad<->dCDF through the shared electron = alpha x alpha = alpha^2  (2 EM vertices)
  So M2 = (dyad scale T_c) x (EM handshake alpha^2). Independent of the value -> not circular.
  Total: E_b = 1/2 alpha_c^2 * alpha^2 T_c = (9/2) alpha^4 T_c ;  alpha^4 = (dCDF binding a_c^2)x(handshake a^2)

